        "titulo": "Strong participles of group 1, step by step",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: STRONG (irregular) verbs form the Partizip II with «ge-» + stem + «-EN» (and not «-t»). STEP 2: in GROUP 1, the vowel of the stem stays the SAME as in the infinitive: schlafen → geschlafen; laufen → gelaufen; fahren → gefahren; tragen → getragen; geben → gegeben; essen → gegessen; lesen → gelesen; sehen → gesehen; kommen → gekommen. STEP 3: there is no umlaut in the participle: «du fährst», but «gefahren». STEP 4: careful: «fahren», «laufen» and «kommen» use «sein» in the Perfekt (see lesson 23); for now, learn only the form of the participle. STEP 5: always learn the infinitive together with the participle: «sehen — gesehen». Memorising the pairs is the way.",
        "comparacao": "English also has irregular participles («done», «said», «seen»). In German the rule is: regular verbs in -t, strong verbs in -en (like English «eaten», «given», «driven»).",
